#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: [no an]
#> pause: 45
#> must:    A stately pleasure dome decree:   [no an]
#> must:    Down to a sunless sea.   [no an]
#> must: In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
#> not: ran   [no an]
#> not: man   [no an]
#> source: /an/!{
# 18. ! means "don't", and { } groups commands under one address. McMahon 3.6
# An address followed by ! applies the function to every line the address
# does NOT select. { starts a group: all commands up to the matching } run
# (or are skipped) together under the address of the {. Here the two lines
# without "an" are indented and marked; the three that have it are untouched.
# Try: remove the ! and the other three lines are the ones marked.
/an/!{
  s/^/   /
  s/$/   [no an]/
}

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
